 "_about": "Which control in each task records a learner's own answer. Read by scripts/build-outline.mjs, which stamps data-commit on a control that exists in the page's markup and data-commit-in on the task root when the control is built by script. One task is one earned action. null means the task has no answer to commit (a sandbox, an explorer, a demonstration, a copy button): its section shows the neutral dot. 'needs' names a field that must hold text for the commit to count, so a lock-and-reveal with an empty box is a reveal, not a commit. Rules: C1 a lock, commit, check or record button counts and the options before it do not; C2 where there is no such button, choosing an option counts; C3 in a sorter, placing into a bucket counts; C4 a checklist or self-report field counts on change; never a reveal, show, run, copy, reset or key button.",
